t best plunge the Get into chaos or at worst out destroy the tribe either way the if the Get is gong to Hel because of the cults actions then they are gonna drag the cult down with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T00:42:09-07:00","id":1543189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543142-if-you-tasked-with-writing-the-w5-is-fake-supplement-how-would-you-do-it?p=1543186#post1543186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well to add to that maybe include the Cult of Fenris whose actually a large remnants of the Swords of Heimdall who somehow stumbled across a ritual that they believe could expunge the Weak parts of they patron Fenris to leave him more &quot;pure&quot; but would actually A) split him into two haves like in Purgatory or B) render him inactive or even outright kill him. Either way the &quot;success&quot; of the ritual would at best plunge the Get into chaos or at worst out destroy the tribe either way the if the Get is gong to Hel because of the cults actions then they are gonna drag the cult down with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's playing way too much into Shit That Karim Wanted, so I probably wouldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T01:32:40-07:00","id":1543190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543142-if-you-tasked-with-writing-the-w5-is-fake-supplement-how-would-you-do-it?p=1543189#post1543189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's playing way too much into Shit That Karim Wanted, so I probably wouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean? The way I wrote up the Cult it's a sperate thing from the Get and are a bunch of ideiots who would hurt they own Paton sprit while bemoaning the fact that the tribe has lost touch with they tradition than admit that they brought everything on them selves. while the rest of the Get thinks they either a bunch fanatics who don't know when to quit or pawns to the wrym. Either way it clearly show that the Get is totally against the Cult and even if the succeed then survivors of the Get will scour the Cult off the face of Gaia than meekly fade into the night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 10-06-2024, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T03:52:59-07:00","id":1543194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543142-if-you-tasked-with-writing-the-w5-is-fake-supplement-how-would-you-do-it?p=1543158#post1543158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even when I discuss W5, the point is discussing W5. I\u2019ve already lost interest in WtE because it seems to simply exist to piss on W5 instead of being its own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? I'm the only one that's comparing W5 to WtE while the WtE team as a whole seems to be ignoring W5 besides the project manger replying to a tumbler thread.. If my post gives you a bad impression of WtE then I'm sorry about that Like generally I'm really sorry about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T11:12:15-07:00","id":1543202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543142-if-you-tasked-with-writing-the-w5-is-fake-supplement-how-would-you-do-it?p=1543194#post1543194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How so? I'm the only one that's comparing W5 to WtE while the WtE team as a whole seems to be ignoring W5 besides the project manger replying to a tumbler thread.. If my post gives you a bad impression of WtE then I'm sorry about that Like generally I'm really sorry about that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It my be because you've had these last few months. a tendancy to pop in basically any thread where W5 is mentioned in a negative light, which is to say all of them, in order to make the promotion of WtE. <br /> <br /> I almost decided to PM you on the overload of mentions of WtE while you already had a tgread dedicated to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T18:57:10-07:00","id":1543238,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25848\" data-vbnamecard=\"25848\">MrornX</a> basically what Nyremne said.<br /> <br /> Threads about W5 are about W5, mentioning WtE there doesn\u2019t do it any favors.<br /> <br /> Also, this very thread may end up being entirely locked at any time because this is just edition-warrying/hating.<br /> <br /> You may hate W5, most of us do, but you\u2019re going overboard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T05:43:10-07:00","id":1543261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543142-if-you-tasked-with-writing-the-w5-is-fake-supplement-how-would-you-do-it?p=1543194#post1543194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How so? I'm the only one that's comparing W5 to WtE while the WtE team as a whole seems to be ignoring W5 besides the project manger replying to a tumbler thread.. If my post gives you a bad impression of WtE then I'm sorry about that Like generally I'm really sorry about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thirding this, as interested as I am in W:tE and as much as I dislike W5 it's getting tiresome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T16:03:28-07:00","id":1543293,"title":"","content":"I need to set the record straight on a few things, first and foremost of which is that MrornX is not someone working on W:tE but is a (very) enthusiastic fan. I appreciate the enthusiasm for W:tE and I admit its a little weird waking up and seeing people so passionately speaking of something I'm writing (in a good way,) but I have to chime in with others and say I'm not okay with W:tE and my words being used to edition war. I'm also uncomfortable with a figurative reply to a hypothetical question submitted on my unofficial Tumblr being used in this manner; my opinions on my personal blog are my own, and if you want something more substantive and citably relevant to W:tE, please cite the official blog.<br /> <br /> Since I first began initially outlining this project, w5 had just barely been announced, and it has been my intention since day 1 to make this series one that meshes and compliments all the Werewolf editions. That ethical imperative hasn't changed since then, even if my criticisms of the game have. My affection for Werewolf is a lifelong one that will likely never end. My criticisms, first and foremost, are directed not just at 5th edition but 20th and revised as well, in that with each successive release, fewer tools are being provided to Storytellers to build stories and manage tables, the pathos of the setting has been diluted for raw mechanics crunch, and some of the magic that's kept me entranced by the game since the 90s has been lost while also making the tabletop a bit scarier for queer fans like me (in a most non-non-heinous way.) I have many (many) criticisms of the latest edition, but I don't think its fair to make the fans suffer for it. This is where the Essentals comes in with the title. We've held on to the essentials that can be preserved across all editions to present a game of timeless cultural substance and horror at the forefront, so this game will retain its cultural value regardless of future editions that come out.<br /> <br /> When JF Sambrano called out the actions of Karim Muammar while working on 5th edition, he made abundantly clear that edition warring isn't what he wants and that the focus of the worst of atrocities isn't the mechanics, the lack of content, and questionable graphics, but the anti-indigenous culture fostered by the individuals who took over the project. His writing was an open challenge to the World of Darkness to do better. That the culture that allowed this to transpire <i>isn't okay. </i>That's never changed for me either, and, for the record, JF Sambrano is now not just writing on the WtE project but also a playtester.<br /> <br /> This same drive is reflected in the words of the passionate writers who have contributed to this project. Everything about the writing in this project is an expression of love, and I think it will speak for itself, but in case it does need to be said, this project aims to build something rather than tear it down; the world is already a messed up enough place to warrant a game about it. The book offers no unkind words to the 5th edition of Werewolf and, indeed, has a dedicated section to systems translation so w5 tabletops can assimilate the deep lore across all editions into their tabletop. I hope I won't have to repeat this to the rest of you, but I want W:tE to be a challenge to eachother to build something better rather than continue drawing barbed wire and digging trenches.<br /> <br /> This is all to say: please don't let a fan's overenthusiasm debase the amount of love going into this project. Thanks for reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T07:18:49-07:00","id":1543422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The book offers no unkind words to the 5th edition of Werewolf and, indeed, has a <b>dedicated section to systems translation so w5 tabletops</b> can assimilate the deep lore across all editions into their tabletop. </div> </div> </div>Your sentiments in general have piqued my interest in this project, I've not followed it closely as I do not have a Tumblr account. I am one of the legacy players that feels that the setting of W5 is off the mark. That said I do like some of the mechanical changes made. With your project I should have more help in running my Werewolf: the Forsaken/Apocalypse mash up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}